id: regexp/literals/s1-s5-names/0001
area: regexp
op: IsValidRegularExpressionLiteral
in: str:"[\\k<a>](?<a>x)" str:""
out: value: bool:true
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: bool:true
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: bool:true
divergence.broiler-js: row S5 as revised 2026-11-01 (owner's decision D-s5): \k in a class beside a named group without u or v, [\k<a>](?<a>x) and [\k](?<a>x), by the constructor, a literal never evaluated and an exec; Broiler.JS answers refused, a SyntaxError "invalid named reference": RegExpGroupNames refuses a \k inside a class whenever the pattern holds a group name, where B.1.2's ClassEscape reads ~NamedCaptureGroups and admits k as an identity escape, the outcome this vector's per-engine field holds (regexpref's reading, which revision 31 took); a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081, by D-s5); answered by SJL-11.5, which deletes RegExpGroupNames' regular-expression prechecks (decision D20)
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-primary-expression-regular-expression-literals-static-semantics-early-errors spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-isvalidregularexpressionliteral spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-parsepattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regular-expressions-patterns ref:regexpref@1
script: (function () { return /[\k<a>](?<a>x)/; }), true
note: correspondence rows S1, S2a, S5: group names and references in a literal; /[\k<a>](?<a>x)/ never evaluated: accepted; the outcome holds with B.1.2 alone (without Annex B: error: SyntaxError); Annex B is required of a web-browser host and optional for any other; both engines answer B.1.2's patterns (Broiler.VM's JSD-0081, requirement R5, Annex B syntax where the specification allows it, and bundle sjl-11-001's correspondence, rows S4 and S7, same in both), so each engine's expectation is B.1.2's outcome
since: 31

