id: regexp/literals/s9b-literal-grammar/0001
area: regexp
op: RegularExpressionLiteral, eval code
in: str:"/a[bc\\" str:"indirect"
out: error: SyntaxError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-vm: row S9b: a literal ending in a backslash at the end of eval code, /a[bc\, by direct and indirect eval; Broiler.VM answers an EvalError ("the artifact provider did not supply a program"): the scan moves past the end of the source (CP/SliceTokenizer.cs:2227 at aaa39fb); a correction of Broiler.VM outside SJL-11 (JSD-0081: the scanner is the front end's, SJL-12's and SJL-13's); answered by the front end's cut-over to the shared syntax library (SJL-13), not by SJL-11.4
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-literals-regular-expression-literals spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-performeval
script: (0, eval)("/a[bc\\")
note: correspondence row S9b: indirect: RegularExpressionLiteral's own grammar refuses the source, a SyntaxError; the expected value is read from the clauses, which regexpref does not model
since: 31

id: regexp/literals/s9b-literal-grammar/0002
